window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b340-57fb3bfa5cec441f.json"]={sha256:"57fb3bfa5cec441fe416625ddabfddaca07d9638ee13c253afed9bafdf6bdf42",value:{"id":"b340","title":"長焊鋼軌應力放散","titleEn":"Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"長焊鋼軌應力放散以「連續焊軌中性溫度約束與位移證據」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。連續鋼軌的熱伸縮被扣件與道床約束，軌溫與應力自由溫度的差才是熱力判斷的起點；軌道橫向阻力及初始不整也影響穩定性。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops neutral temperature restraint and displacement evidence in welded rail through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Fastenings and ballast restrain thermal rail movement; the difference between rail temperature and stress-free temperature starts the force assessment, while lateral resistance and initial misalignment also govern stability. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["軌溫量測","Rail temperature"],["自由伸縮","Free expansion"],["縱向約束","Longitudinal restraint"],["中性狀態","Neutral state"],["軌道穩定","Track stability"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["軌溫量測","自由伸縮","縱向約束","中性狀態","軌道穩定"],"labelsEn":["Rail temperature","Free expansion","Longitudinal restraint","Neutral state","Track stability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=25.3 mm。模型邊界：均勻軌溫、定熱膨脹係數及無軸向約束；忽略溫度梯度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K；y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa。只把 E 增加百分之十，y=66.4125 MPa。模型邊界：線彈性桿完全軸向約束；結果為應力大小，升溫為壓縮、降溫為拉伸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=25.3 mm. Boundary: Uniform rail temperature, constant expansion coefficient and no axial restraint; temperature gradients are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K; y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa. Increasing only E with a ten-percent increase gives y=66.4125 MPa. Boundary: A fully axially restrained elastic bar; the result is stress magnitude, compressive for heating and tensile for cooling; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b340-v16-s1","title":"自由鋼軌伸長與全約束熱應力","titleEn":"Free rail expansion & Fully restrained thermal stress","description":"本階段聚焦「自由鋼軌伸長」與「全約束熱應力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Free rail expansion\" and \"Fully restrained thermal stress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b340-v16-01","title":"自由鋼軌伸長：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Free rail expansion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「自由鋼軌伸長」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Free rail expansion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"無約束鋼軌可以以長度變化釋放熱應變。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 25.3 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻軌溫、定熱膨脹係數及無軸向約束；忽略溫度梯度。使用軌溫和端部位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「自由鋼軌伸長」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Unrestrained rail releases thermal strain through a change in length. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 25.3 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform rail temperature, constant expansion coefficient and no axial restraint; temperature gradients are omitted. Use rail temperature and endpoint displacement as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Free rail expansion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「自由鋼軌伸長」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Free rail expansion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-01-k1","title":"自由鋼軌伸長","titleEn":"Free rail expansion","text":"無約束鋼軌可以以長度變化釋放熱應變。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 25.3 mm。","textEn":"Unrestrained rail releases thermal strain through a change in length. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自由鋼軌伸長」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Free rail expansion\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設","無約束鋼軌可以以長度變化釋放熱應變。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior.","Unrestrained rail releases thermal strain through a change in length.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"無約束鋼軌可以以長度變化釋放熱應變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Unrestrained rail releases thermal strain through a change in length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b340-v16-02","title":"自由鋼軌伸長：定量估算","titleEn":"Free rail expansion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「自由鋼軌伸長」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Free rail expansion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=25.3 mm。模型邊界：均勻軌溫、定熱膨脹係數及無軸向約束；忽略溫度梯度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=25.3 mm. Boundary: Uniform rail temperature, constant expansion coefficient and no axial restraint; temperature gradients are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以軌溫和端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼條兩端位移計、標距及多點溫度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use rail temperature and endpoint displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=25.3 mm。模型邊界：均勻軌溫、定熱膨脹係數及無軸向約束；忽略溫度梯度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=25.3 mm. Boundary: Uniform rail temperature, constant expansion coefficient and no axial restraint; temperature gradients are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「自由鋼軌伸長」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Free rail expansion\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=100 m, dT=20 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=23 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b340-v16-03","title":"自由鋼軌伸長：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Free rail expansion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「自由鋼軌伸長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Free rail expansion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以軌溫和端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼條兩端位移計、標距及多點溫度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「自由鋼軌伸長」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use rail temperature and endpoint displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model-bar endpoint displacement gauges, gauge length and distributed temperature records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Free rail expansion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「自由鋼軌伸長」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻軌溫、定熱膨脹係數及無軸向約束；忽略溫度梯度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌溫和端部位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Free rail expansion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform rail temperature, constant expansion coefficient and no axial restraint; temperature gradients are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior. Explain which evidence in rail temperature and endpoint displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以軌溫和端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼條兩端位移計、標距及多點溫度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「自由鋼軌伸長」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use rail temperature and endpoint displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model-bar endpoint displacement gauges, gauge length and distributed temperature records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Free rail expansion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「自由鋼軌伸長」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻軌溫、定熱膨脹係數及無軸向約束；忽略溫度梯度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌溫和端部位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Free rail expansion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform rail temperature, constant expansion coefficient and no axial restraint; temperature gradients are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior. Explain which evidence in rail temperature and endpoint displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「自由鋼軌伸長」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Free rail expansion\"?","options":["本單元以軌溫和端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼條兩端位移計、標距及多點溫度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲"],"optionsEn":["Use rail temperature and endpoint displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以軌溫和端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型鋼條兩端位移計、標距及多點溫度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use rail temperature and endpoint displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b340-v16-04","title":"自由鋼軌伸長：失效診斷","titleEn":"Free rail expansion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「自由鋼軌伸長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Free rail expansion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設。這個失效與「自由鋼軌伸長」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌溫和端部位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior. This failure and a measurement bias in Free rail expansion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail temperature and endpoint displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用軌溫和端部位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設。這個失效與「自由鋼軌伸長」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌溫和端部位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior. This failure and a measurement bias in Free rail expansion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail temperature and endpoint displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「自由鋼軌伸長」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Free rail expansion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b340-v16-05","title":"全約束熱應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「全約束熱應力」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fully restrained thermal stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"完全約束下軸向熱應變轉成應力。本模型把 E 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 66.4125 MPa。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。線彈性桿完全軸向約束；結果為應力大小，升溫為壓縮、降溫為拉伸。使用軌溫與可追溯應變作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「全約束熱應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Full axial restraint converts thermal strain into stress. In this model, E is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 66.4125 MPa. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. A fully axially restrained elastic bar; the result is stress magnitude, compressive for heating and tensile for cooling. Use rail temperature and traceable strain as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fully restrained thermal stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K；y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K; y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「全約束熱應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fully restrained thermal stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-05-k1","title":"全約束熱應力","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress","text":"完全約束下軸向熱應變轉成應力。本模型把 E 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 66.4125 MPa。","textEn":"Full axial restraint converts thermal strain into stress. In this model, E is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「全約束熱應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fully restrained thermal stress\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力","完全約束下軸向熱應變轉成應力。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.","Full axial restraint converts thermal strain into stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"完全約束下軸向熱應變轉成應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Full axial restraint converts thermal strain into stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b340-v16-06","title":"全約束熱應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「全約束熱應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fully restrained thermal stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K；y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa。只把 E 增加百分之十，y=66.4125 MPa。模型邊界：線彈性桿完全軸向約束；結果為應力大小，升溫為壓縮、降溫為拉伸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K; y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa. Increasing only E with a ten-percent increase gives y=66.4125 MPa. Boundary: A fully axially restrained elastic bar; the result is stress magnitude, compressive for heating and tensile for cooling; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以軌溫與可追溯應變區分模型與觀察，先用合成約束力、截面面積、補償應變與軌溫時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use rail temperature and traceable strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K；y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa。只把 E 增加百分之十，y=66.4125 MPa。模型邊界：線彈性桿完全軸向約束；結果為應力大小，升溫為壓縮、降溫為拉伸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K; y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa. Increasing only E with a ten-percent increase gives y=66.4125 MPa. Boundary: A fully axially restrained elastic bar; the result is stress magnitude, compressive for heating and tensile for cooling; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「全約束熱應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fully restrained thermal stress\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K; y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K；y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=25 K; y=E*1000*alpha*dT=60.375 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b340-v16-07","title":"全約束熱應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「全約束熱應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fully restrained thermal stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以軌溫與可追溯應變區分模型與觀察，先用合成約束力、截面面積、補償應變與軌溫時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「全約束熱應力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use rail temperature and traceable strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic restraint force, area, compensated strain and rail-temperature histories, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Fully restrained thermal stress. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「全約束熱應力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線彈性桿完全軸向約束；結果為應力大小，升溫為壓縮、降溫為拉伸如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌溫與可追溯應變說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Fully restrained thermal stress, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: A fully axially restrained elastic bar; the result is stress magnitude, compressive for heating and tensile for cooling. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate. Explain which evidence in rail temperature and traceable strain distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以軌溫與可追溯應變區分模型與觀察，先用合成約束力、截面面積、補償應變與軌溫時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「全約束熱應力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use rail temperature and traceable strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic restraint force, area, compensated strain and rail-temperature histories, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Fully restrained thermal stress. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「全約束熱應力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線彈性桿完全軸向約束；結果為應力大小，升溫為壓縮、降溫為拉伸如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌溫與可追溯應變說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Fully restrained thermal stress, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: A fully axially restrained elastic bar; the result is stress magnitude, compressive for heating and tensile for cooling. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate. Explain which evidence in rail temperature and traceable strain distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「全約束熱應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fully restrained thermal stress\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以軌溫與可追溯應變區分模型與觀察，先用合成約束力、截面面積、補償應變與軌溫時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use rail temperature and traceable strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以軌溫與可追溯應變區分模型與觀察，先用合成約束力、截面面積、補償應變與軌溫時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use rail temperature and traceable strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b340-v16-08","title":"全約束熱應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「全約束熱應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fully restrained thermal stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移。這個失效與「全約束熱應力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌溫與可追溯應變，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate. This failure and a measurement bias in Fully restrained thermal stress can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail temperature and traceable strain rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用軌溫與可追溯應變作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移。這個失效與「全約束熱應力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌溫與可追溯應變，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate. This failure and a measurement bias in Fully restrained thermal stress can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail temperature and traceable strain rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「全約束熱應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fully restrained thermal stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力","中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.","Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b340-v16-s2","title":"熱軸力換算與軌溫量測誤差","titleEn":"Thermal axial-force conversion & Rail-temperature error propagation","description":"本階段聚焦「熱軸力換算」與「軌溫量測誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thermal axial-force conversion\" and \"Rail-temperature error propagation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b340-v16-09","title":"熱軸力換算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal axial-force conversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「熱軸力換算」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermal axial-force conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"軸力等於平均應力乘有效斷面，左右兩軌須分別核對。本模型把 sigma 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 501.6 kN。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。應力沿有效斷面均勻；只算單根鋼軌的軸力。使用斷面損耗與軸向應變作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「熱軸力換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Axial force equals mean stress times effective area, with each rail checked separately. In this model, sigma is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 501.6 kN. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Stress is uniform over the effective section; force is for one rail only. Use section loss and axial strain as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thermal axial-force conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2；y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2; y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「熱軸力換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thermal axial-force conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-09-k1","title":"熱軸力換算","titleEn":"Thermal axial-force conversion","text":"軸力等於平均應力乘有效斷面，左右兩軌須分別核對。本模型把 sigma 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 501.6 kN。","textEn":"Axial force equals mean stress times effective area, with each rail checked separately. In this model, sigma is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱軸力換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal axial-force conversion\" is correct?","options":["軸力等於平均應力乘有效斷面，左右兩軌須分別核對。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性"],"optionsEn":["Axial force equals mean stress times effective area, with each rail checked separately.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative."],"answer":0,"explanation":"軸力等於平均應力乘有效斷面，左右兩軌須分別核對。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Axial force equals mean stress times effective area, with each rail checked separately. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b340-v16-10","title":"熱軸力換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal axial-force conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「熱軸力換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermal axial-force conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2；y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN。只把 sigma 增加百分之十，y=501.6 kN。模型邊界：應力沿有效斷面均勻；只算單根鋼軌的軸力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2; y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN. Increasing only sigma with a ten-percent increase gives y=501.6 kN. Boundary: Stress is uniform over the effective section; force is for one rail only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以斷面損耗與軸向應變區分模型與觀察，先用模型截面尺寸、磨耗面積及多位置軸向應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use section loss and axial strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2；y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN。只把 sigma 增加百分之十，y=501.6 kN。模型邊界：應力沿有效斷面均勻；只算單根鋼軌的軸力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2; y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN. Increasing only sigma with a ten-percent increase gives y=501.6 kN. Boundary: Stress is uniform over the effective section; force is for one rail only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「熱軸力換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal axial-force conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2；y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2; y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2；y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: sigma=60 MPa, A=7600 mm2; y=sigma*A/1000=456 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b340-v16-11","title":"熱軸力換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal axial-force conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「熱軸力換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thermal axial-force conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以斷面損耗與軸向應變區分模型與觀察，先用模型截面尺寸、磨耗面積及多位置軸向應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「熱軸力換算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use section loss and axial strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model section dimensions, worn area and axial strain at multiple locations, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal axial-force conversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「熱軸力換算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出應力沿有效斷面均勻；只算單根鋼軌的軸力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力造成偏離的合成觀察，以斷面損耗與軸向應變說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal axial-force conversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Stress is uniform over the effective section; force is for one rail only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force. Explain which evidence in section loss and axial strain distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以斷面損耗與軸向應變區分模型與觀察，先用模型截面尺寸、磨耗面積及多位置軸向應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「熱軸力換算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use section loss and axial strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model section dimensions, worn area and axial strain at multiple locations, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal axial-force conversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「熱軸力換算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出應力沿有效斷面均勻；只算單根鋼軌的軸力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力造成偏離的合成觀察，以斷面損耗與軸向應變說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal axial-force conversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Stress is uniform over the effective section; force is for one rail only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force. Explain which evidence in section loss and axial strain distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「熱軸力換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal axial-force conversion\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一","本單元以斷面損耗與軸向應變區分模型與觀察，先用模型截面尺寸、磨耗面積及多位置軸向應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line.","Use section loss and axial strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以斷面損耗與軸向應變區分模型與觀察，先用模型截面尺寸、磨耗面積及多位置軸向應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use section loss and axial strain to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b340-v16-12","title":"熱軸力換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal axial-force conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「熱軸力換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thermal axial-force conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力。這個失效與「熱軸力換算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查斷面損耗與軸向應變，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal axial-force conversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check section loss and axial strain rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用斷面損耗與軸向應變作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力。這個失效與「熱軸力換算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查斷面損耗與軸向應變，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal axial-force conversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check section loss and axial strain rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱軸力換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal axial-force conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性"],"optionsEn":["Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative."],"answer":0,"explanation":"磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b340-v16-13","title":"軌溫量測誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rail-temperature error propagation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「軌溫量測誤差」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rail-temperature error propagation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"溫度誤差經彈性係數直接傳到熱應力估計。本模型把 E 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 5.313 MPa。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。只傳播軌溫誤差；彈性係數、熱膨脹係數及約束皆視為已知。使用兩種接觸式溫度量測作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「軌溫量測誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Temperature error propagates through stiffness into thermal-stress estimation. In this model, E is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 5.313 MPa. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Only rail-temperature error is propagated; modulus, expansion coefficient and restraint are treated as known. Use two contact-temperature measurements as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rail-temperature error propagation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K；y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K; y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「軌溫量測誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rail-temperature error propagation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-13-k1","title":"軌溫量測誤差","titleEn":"Rail-temperature error propagation","text":"溫度誤差經彈性係數直接傳到熱應力估計。本模型把 E 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 5.313 MPa。","textEn":"Temperature error propagates through stiffness into thermal-stress estimation. In this model, E is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軌溫量測誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rail-temperature error propagation\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性","溫度誤差經彈性係數直接傳到熱應力估計。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative.","Temperature error propagates through stiffness into thermal-stress estimation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溫度誤差經彈性係數直接傳到熱應力估計。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Temperature error propagates through stiffness into thermal-stress estimation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b340-v16-14","title":"軌溫量測誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Rail-temperature error propagation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軌溫量測誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rail-temperature error propagation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K；y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa。只把 E 增加百分之十，y=5.313 MPa。模型邊界：只傳播軌溫誤差；彈性係數、熱膨脹係數及約束皆視為已知；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K; y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa. Increasing only E with a ten-percent increase gives y=5.313 MPa. Boundary: Only rail-temperature error is propagated; modulus, expansion coefficient and restraint are treated as known; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以兩種接觸式溫度量測區分模型與觀察，先用同步雙溫度計、溫度校準紀錄及合成應力估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use two contact-temperature measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K；y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa。只把 E 增加百分之十，y=5.313 MPa。模型邊界：只傳播軌溫誤差；彈性係數、熱膨脹係數及約束皆視為已知；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K; y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa. Increasing only E with a ten-percent increase gives y=5.313 MPa. Boundary: Only rail-temperature error is propagated; modulus, expansion coefficient and restraint are treated as known; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軌溫量測誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rail-temperature error propagation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K; y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K；y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: E=210 GPa, alpha=0.0000115 1/K, uT=2 K; y=E*1000*alpha*uT=4.83 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b340-v16-15","title":"軌溫量測誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rail-temperature error propagation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「軌溫量測誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rail-temperature error propagation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以兩種接觸式溫度量測區分模型與觀察，先用同步雙溫度計、溫度校準紀錄及合成應力估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌溫量測誤差」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use two contact-temperature measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired synchronous thermometers, calibration records and synthetic stress estimates, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rail-temperature error propagation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「軌溫量測誤差」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出只傳播軌溫誤差；彈性係數、熱膨脹係數及約束皆視為已知如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性造成偏離的合成觀察，以兩種接觸式溫度量測說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rail-temperature error propagation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Only rail-temperature error is propagated; modulus, expansion coefficient and restraint are treated as known. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative. Explain which evidence in two contact-temperature measurements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以兩種接觸式溫度量測區分模型與觀察，先用同步雙溫度計、溫度校準紀錄及合成應力估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌溫量測誤差」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use two contact-temperature measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired synchronous thermometers, calibration records and synthetic stress estimates, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rail-temperature error propagation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「軌溫量測誤差」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出只傳播軌溫誤差；彈性係數、熱膨脹係數及約束皆視為已知如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性造成偏離的合成觀察，以兩種接觸式溫度量測說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rail-temperature error propagation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Only rail-temperature error is propagated; modulus, expansion coefficient and restraint are treated as known. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative. Explain which evidence in two contact-temperature measurements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軌溫量測誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rail-temperature error propagation\"?","options":["本單元以兩種接觸式溫度量測區分模型與觀察，先用同步雙溫度計、溫度校準紀錄及合成應力估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設"],"optionsEn":["Use two contact-temperature measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以兩種接觸式溫度量測區分模型與觀察，先用同步雙溫度計、溫度校準紀錄及合成應力估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use two contact-temperature measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b340-v16-16","title":"軌溫量測誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rail-temperature error propagation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軌溫量測誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rail-temperature error propagation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性。這個失效與「軌溫量測誤差」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查兩種接觸式溫度量測，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative. This failure and a measurement bias in Rail-temperature error propagation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check two contact-temperature measurements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用兩種接觸式溫度量測作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性。這個失效與「軌溫量測誤差」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查兩種接觸式溫度量測，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative. This failure and a measurement bias in Rail-temperature error propagation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check two contact-temperature measurements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軌溫量測誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rail-temperature error propagation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b340-v16-s3","title":"扣件阻力累積與溫差等效位移","titleEn":"Fastening resistance accumulation & Temperature-equivalent displacement","description":"本階段聚焦「扣件阻力累積」與「溫差等效位移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fastening resistance accumulation\" and \"Temperature-equivalent displacement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b340-v16-17","title":"扣件阻力累積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fastening resistance accumulation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「扣件阻力累積」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fastening resistance accumulation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻分布縱向阻力積分後形成可傳遞軸力的量級。本模型把 r 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 264 kN。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。全長均勻且已動員的縱向阻力；不是未滑移狀態的彈性剛度。使用沿線相對滑移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「扣件阻力累積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Integrating uniform longitudinal resistance gives a transferable-force scale. In this model, r is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 264 kN. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform longitudinal resistance is fully mobilized along the length; it is not pre-slip elastic stiffness. Use relative slip along the line as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fastening resistance accumulation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=8 kN/m, L=30 m；y=r*L=240 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=8 kN/m, L=30 m; y=r*L=240 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「扣件阻力累積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fastening resistance accumulation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-17-k1","title":"扣件阻力累積","titleEn":"Fastening resistance accumulation","text":"均勻分布縱向阻力積分後形成可傳遞軸力的量級。本模型把 r 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 264 kN。","textEn":"Integrating uniform longitudinal resistance gives a transferable-force scale. In this model, r is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「扣件阻力累積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fastening resistance accumulation\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差","均勻分布縱向阻力積分後形成可傳遞軸力的量級。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.","Integrating uniform longitudinal resistance gives a transferable-force scale."],"answer":2,"explanation":"均勻分布縱向阻力積分後形成可傳遞軸力的量級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Integrating uniform longitudinal resistance gives a transferable-force scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b340-v16-18","title":"扣件阻力累積：定量估算","titleEn":"Fastening resistance accumulation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「扣件阻力累積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fastening resistance accumulation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=8 kN/m, L=30 m；y=r*L=240 kN。只把 r 增加百分之十，y=264 kN。模型邊界：全長均勻且已動員的縱向阻力；不是未滑移狀態的彈性剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=8 kN/m, L=30 m; y=r*L=240 kN. Increasing only r with a ten-percent increase gives y=264 kN. Boundary: Uniform longitudinal resistance is fully mobilized along the length; it is not pre-slip elastic stiffness; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以沿線相對滑移區分模型與觀察，先用多段模型滑移量與相對應縱向反力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use relative slip along the line to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=8 kN/m, L=30 m；y=r*L=240 kN。只把 r 增加百分之十，y=264 kN。模型邊界：全長均勻且已動員的縱向阻力；不是未滑移狀態的彈性剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=8 kN/m, L=30 m; y=r*L=240 kN. Increasing only r with a ten-percent increase gives y=264 kN. Boundary: Uniform longitudinal resistance is fully mobilized along the length; it is not pre-slip elastic stiffness; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「扣件阻力累積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fastening resistance accumulation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=8 kN/m, L=30 m；y=r*L=240 kN。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=8 kN/m, L=30 m; y=r*L=240 kN.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=8 kN/m, L=30 m；y=r*L=240 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=8 kN/m, L=30 m; y=r*L=240 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b340-v16-19","title":"扣件阻力累積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fastening resistance accumulation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「扣件阻力累積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fastening resistance accumulation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以沿線相對滑移區分模型與觀察，先用多段模型滑移量與相對應縱向反力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「扣件阻力累積」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use relative slip along the line to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using segment-by-segment model slip and corresponding longitudinal reactions, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Fastening resistance accumulation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「扣件阻力累積」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出全長均勻且已動員的縱向阻力；不是未滑移狀態的彈性剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制造成偏離的合成觀察，以沿線相對滑移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Fastening resistance accumulation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform longitudinal resistance is fully mobilized along the length; it is not pre-slip elastic stiffness. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms. Explain which evidence in relative slip along the line distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以沿線相對滑移區分模型與觀察，先用多段模型滑移量與相對應縱向反力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「扣件阻力累積」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use relative slip along the line to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using segment-by-segment model slip and corresponding longitudinal reactions, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Fastening resistance accumulation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「扣件阻力累積」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出全長均勻且已動員的縱向阻力；不是未滑移狀態的彈性剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制造成偏離的合成觀察，以沿線相對滑移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Fastening resistance accumulation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform longitudinal resistance is fully mobilized along the length; it is not pre-slip elastic stiffness. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms. Explain which evidence in relative slip along the line distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「扣件阻力累積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fastening resistance accumulation\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以沿線相對滑移區分模型與觀察，先用多段模型滑移量與相對應縱向反力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use relative slip along the line to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以沿線相對滑移區分模型與觀察，先用多段模型滑移量與相對應縱向反力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use relative slip along the line to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b340-v16-20","title":"扣件阻力累積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fastening resistance accumulation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「扣件阻力累積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fastening resistance accumulation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制。這個失效與「扣件阻力累積」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查沿線相對滑移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms. This failure and a measurement bias in Fastening resistance accumulation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check relative slip along the line rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用沿線相對滑移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制。這個失效與「扣件阻力累積」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查沿線相對滑移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms. This failure and a measurement bias in Fastening resistance accumulation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check relative slip along the line rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「扣件阻力累積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fastening resistance accumulation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差","把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.","Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b340-v16-21","title":"溫差等效位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Temperature-equivalent displacement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「溫差等效位移」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Temperature-equivalent displacement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"等效熱位移只能在指定長度與邊界下解讀。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 12.144 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。同一已知標距的自由熱位移；不把它視為有約束鋼軌的實際位移。使用標距及基準端點作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溫差等效位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Equivalent thermal movement is meaningful only for the stated length and boundaries. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 12.144 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Free thermal movement over a known gauge length; it is not actual movement of a restrained rail. Use gauge length and reference endpoints as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Temperature-equivalent displacement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「溫差等效位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Temperature-equivalent displacement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-21-k1","title":"溫差等效位移","titleEn":"Temperature-equivalent displacement","text":"等效熱位移只能在指定長度與邊界下解讀。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 12.144 mm。","textEn":"Equivalent thermal movement is meaningful only for the stated length and boundaries. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫差等效位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Temperature-equivalent displacement\" is correct?","options":["等效熱位移只能在指定長度與邊界下解讀。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變"],"optionsEn":["Equivalent thermal movement is meaningful only for the stated length and boundaries.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"等效熱位移只能在指定長度與邊界下解讀。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Equivalent thermal movement is meaningful only for the stated length and boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b340-v16-22","title":"溫差等效位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Temperature-equivalent displacement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「溫差等效位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Temperature-equivalent displacement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=12.144 mm。模型邊界：同一已知標距的自由熱位移；不把它視為有約束鋼軌的實際位移；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=12.144 mm. Boundary: Free thermal movement over a known gauge length; it is not actual movement of a restrained rail; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以標距及基準端點區分模型與觀察，先用固定基準標記、模型標距及平均鋼條溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use gauge length and reference endpoints to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=12.144 mm。模型邊界：同一已知標距的自由熱位移；不把它視為有約束鋼軌的實際位移；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=12.144 mm. Boundary: Free thermal movement over a known gauge length; it is not actual movement of a restrained rail; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫差等效位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Temperature-equivalent displacement\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=80 m, dT=12 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=11.04 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b340-v16-23","title":"溫差等效位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Temperature-equivalent displacement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「溫差等效位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Temperature-equivalent displacement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以標距及基準端點區分模型與觀察，先用固定基準標記、模型標距及平均鋼條溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫差等效位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use gauge length and reference endpoints to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using fixed reference markers, model gauge length and mean bar temperature, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Temperature-equivalent displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「溫差等效位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同一已知標距的自由熱位移；不把它視為有約束鋼軌的實際位移如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差造成偏離的合成觀察，以標距及基準端點說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Temperature-equivalent displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Free thermal movement over a known gauge length; it is not actual movement of a restrained rail. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change. Explain which evidence in gauge length and reference endpoints distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以標距及基準端點區分模型與觀察，先用固定基準標記、模型標距及平均鋼條溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫差等效位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use gauge length and reference endpoints to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using fixed reference markers, model gauge length and mean bar temperature, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Temperature-equivalent displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「溫差等效位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同一已知標距的自由熱位移；不把它視為有約束鋼軌的實際位移如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差造成偏離的合成觀察，以標距及基準端點說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Temperature-equivalent displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Free thermal movement over a known gauge length; it is not actual movement of a restrained rail. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change. Explain which evidence in gauge length and reference endpoints distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫差等效位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Temperature-equivalent displacement\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力","本單元以標距及基準端點區分模型與觀察，先用固定基準標記、模型標距及平均鋼條溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.","Use gauge length and reference endpoints to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以標距及基準端點區分模型與觀察，先用固定基準標記、模型標距及平均鋼條溫度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use gauge length and reference endpoints to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b340-v16-24","title":"溫差等效位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Temperature-equivalent displacement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「溫差等效位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Temperature-equivalent displacement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差。這個失效與「溫差等效位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查標距及基準端點，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change. This failure and a measurement bias in Temperature-equivalent displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check gauge length and reference endpoints rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用標距及基準端點作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差。這個失效與「溫差等效位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查標距及基準端點，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change. This failure and a measurement bias in Temperature-equivalent displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check gauge length and reference endpoints rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫差等效位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Temperature-equivalent displacement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變"],"optionsEn":["Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b340-v16-s4","title":"中性溫差反算與截面溫度梯度","titleEn":"Neutral-temperature difference inversion & Cross-section temperature curvature","description":"本階段聚焦「中性溫差反算」與「截面溫度梯度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Neutral-temperature difference inversion\" and \"Cross-section temperature curvature\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b340-v16-25","title":"中性溫差反算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Neutral-temperature difference inversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「中性溫差反算」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Neutral-temperature difference inversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"應變反算溫差必須先分離機械與熱補償項。本模型把 strain 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 11 K。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。應變是已分離機械載重的熱等效大小；只能反算溫差大小，不能單獨定出中性溫度。使用補償應變計與獨立溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「中性溫差反算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inferring temperature difference from strain requires separating mechanical strain and temperature compensation. In this model, strain is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 11 K. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Strain is an isolated thermal-equivalent magnitude; inversion yields a temperature-difference magnitude, not neutral temperature by itself. Use compensated strain gauges and independent temperature as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Neutral-temperature difference inversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K；y=strain/alpha=10 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K; y=strain/alpha=10 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「中性溫差反算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Neutral-temperature difference inversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-25-k1","title":"中性溫差反算","titleEn":"Neutral-temperature difference inversion","text":"應變反算溫差必須先分離機械與熱補償項。本模型把 strain 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 11 K。","textEn":"Inferring temperature difference from strain requires separating mechanical strain and temperature compensation. In this model, strain is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「中性溫差反算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Neutral-temperature difference inversion\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變","應變反算溫差必須先分離機械與熱補償項。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change.","Inferring temperature difference from strain requires separating mechanical strain and temperature compensation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應變反算溫差必須先分離機械與熱補償項。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inferring temperature difference from strain requires separating mechanical strain and temperature compensation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b340-v16-26","title":"中性溫差反算：定量估算","titleEn":"Neutral-temperature difference inversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「中性溫差反算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Neutral-temperature difference inversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K；y=strain/alpha=10 K。只把 strain 增加百分之十，y=11 K。模型邊界：應變是已分離機械載重的熱等效大小；只能反算溫差大小，不能單獨定出中性溫度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K; y=strain/alpha=10 K. Increasing only strain with a ten-percent increase gives y=11 K. Boundary: Strain is an isolated thermal-equivalent magnitude; inversion yields a temperature-difference magnitude, not neutral temperature by itself; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以補償應變計與獨立溫度區分模型與觀察，先用已知約束的合成應變、獨立溫度及熱漂移零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use compensated strain gauges and independent temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K；y=strain/alpha=10 K。只把 strain 增加百分之十，y=11 K。模型邊界：應變是已分離機械載重的熱等效大小；只能反算溫差大小，不能單獨定出中性溫度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K; y=strain/alpha=10 K. Increasing only strain with a ten-percent increase gives y=11 K. Boundary: Strain is an isolated thermal-equivalent magnitude; inversion yields a temperature-difference magnitude, not neutral temperature by itself; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「中性溫差反算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Neutral-temperature difference inversion\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K；y=strain/alpha=10 K。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K; y=strain/alpha=10 K."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K；y=strain/alpha=10 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: strain=0.000115 1, alpha=0.0000115 1/K; y=strain/alpha=10 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b340-v16-27","title":"中性溫差反算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Neutral-temperature difference inversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「中性溫差反算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Neutral-temperature difference inversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以補償應變計與獨立溫度區分模型與觀察，先用已知約束的合成應變、獨立溫度及熱漂移零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「中性溫差反算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use compensated strain gauges and independent temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic strain with known restraint, independent temperature and thermal-drift zero records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Neutral-temperature difference inversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「中性溫差反算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出應變是已分離機械載重的熱等效大小；只能反算溫差大小，不能單獨定出中性溫度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變造成偏離的合成觀察，以補償應變計與獨立溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Neutral-temperature difference inversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Strain is an isolated thermal-equivalent magnitude; inversion yields a temperature-difference magnitude, not neutral temperature by itself. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change. Explain which evidence in compensated strain gauges and independent temperature distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以補償應變計與獨立溫度區分模型與觀察，先用已知約束的合成應變、獨立溫度及熱漂移零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「中性溫差反算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use compensated strain gauges and independent temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic strain with known restraint, independent temperature and thermal-drift zero records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Neutral-temperature difference inversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「中性溫差反算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出應變是已分離機械載重的熱等效大小；只能反算溫差大小，不能單獨定出中性溫度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變造成偏離的合成觀察，以補償應變計與獨立溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Neutral-temperature difference inversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Strain is an isolated thermal-equivalent magnitude; inversion yields a temperature-difference magnitude, not neutral temperature by itself. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change. Explain which evidence in compensated strain gauges and independent temperature distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「中性溫差反算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Neutral-temperature difference inversion\"?","options":["本單元以補償應變計與獨立溫度區分模型與觀察，先用已知約束的合成應變、獨立溫度及熱漂移零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性"],"optionsEn":["Use compensated strain gauges and independent temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以補償應變計與獨立溫度區分模型與觀察，先用已知約束的合成應變、獨立溫度及熱漂移零點紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use compensated strain gauges and independent temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b340-v16-28","title":"中性溫差反算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Neutral-temperature difference inversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「中性溫差反算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Neutral-temperature difference inversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變。這個失效與「中性溫差反算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查補償應變計與獨立溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change. This failure and a measurement bias in Neutral-temperature difference inversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check compensated strain gauges and independent temperature rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用補償應變計與獨立溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變。這個失效與「中性溫差反算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查補償應變計與獨立溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change. This failure and a measurement bias in Neutral-temperature difference inversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check compensated strain gauges and independent temperature rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「中性溫差反算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Neutral-temperature difference inversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b340-v16-29","title":"截面溫度梯度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cross-section temperature curvature: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「截面溫度梯度」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cross-section temperature curvature” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"線性溫度梯度可形成自由熱曲率，平均溫度不含這項資訊。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.000595294 1/m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。軌高方向線性溫差、均勻材料且自由彎曲；忽略軸向及彎曲約束。使用軌頭與軌底溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「截面溫度梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A linear thermal gradient creates free thermal curvature that mean temperature does not describe. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.000595294 1/m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Linear temperature difference through rail height, uniform material and free bending; axial and bending restraints are omitted. Use rail-head and rail-foot temperatures as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cross-section temperature curvature” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m；y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m; y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「截面溫度梯度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cross-section temperature curvature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-29-k1","title":"截面溫度梯度","titleEn":"Cross-section temperature curvature","text":"線性溫度梯度可形成自由熱曲率，平均溫度不含這項資訊。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.000595294 1/m。","textEn":"A linear thermal gradient creates free thermal curvature that mean temperature does not describe. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「截面溫度梯度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cross-section temperature curvature\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長","線性溫度梯度可形成自由熱曲率，平均溫度不含這項資訊。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.","A linear thermal gradient creates free thermal curvature that mean temperature does not describe."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線性溫度梯度可形成自由熱曲率，平均溫度不含這項資訊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A linear thermal gradient creates free thermal curvature that mean temperature does not describe. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b340-v16-30","title":"截面溫度梯度：定量估算","titleEn":"Cross-section temperature curvature: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「截面溫度梯度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cross-section temperature curvature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m；y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.000595294 1/m。模型邊界：軌高方向線性溫差、均勻材料且自由彎曲；忽略軸向及彎曲約束；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m; y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.000595294 1/m. Boundary: Linear temperature difference through rail height, uniform material and free bending; axial and bending restraints are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以軌頭與軌底溫度區分模型與觀察，先用模型軌頭軌底溫度對及彎曲形狀量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use rail-head and rail-foot temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m；y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.000595294 1/m。模型邊界：軌高方向線性溫差、均勻材料且自由彎曲；忽略軸向及彎曲約束；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m; y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.000595294 1/m. Boundary: Linear temperature difference through rail height, uniform material and free bending; axial and bending restraints are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「截面溫度梯度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cross-section temperature curvature\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m; y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m；y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, dT=8 K, h=0.17 m; y=alpha*dT/h=0.000541176 1/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b340-v16-31","title":"截面溫度梯度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cross-section temperature curvature: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「截面溫度梯度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cross-section temperature curvature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以軌頭與軌底溫度區分模型與觀察，先用模型軌頭軌底溫度對及彎曲形狀量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「截面溫度梯度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use rail-head and rail-foot temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired model head-foot temperatures and measured curvature profile, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cross-section temperature curvature. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「截面溫度梯度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出軌高方向線性溫差、均勻材料且自由彎曲；忽略軸向及彎曲約束如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌頭與軌底溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cross-section temperature curvature, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear temperature difference through rail height, uniform material and free bending; axial and bending restraints are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending. Explain which evidence in rail-head and rail-foot temperatures distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以軌頭與軌底溫度區分模型與觀察，先用模型軌頭軌底溫度對及彎曲形狀量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「截面溫度梯度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use rail-head and rail-foot temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired model head-foot temperatures and measured curvature profile, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cross-section temperature curvature. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「截面溫度梯度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出軌高方向線性溫差、均勻材料且自由彎曲；忽略軸向及彎曲約束如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌頭與軌底溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cross-section temperature curvature, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear temperature difference through rail height, uniform material and free bending; axial and bending restraints are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending. Explain which evidence in rail-head and rail-foot temperatures distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「截面溫度梯度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cross-section temperature curvature\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以軌頭與軌底溫度區分模型與觀察，先用模型軌頭軌底溫度對及彎曲形狀量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use rail-head and rail-foot temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以軌頭與軌底溫度區分模型與觀察，先用模型軌頭軌底溫度對及彎曲形狀量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use rail-head and rail-foot temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b340-v16-32","title":"截面溫度梯度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cross-section temperature curvature: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「截面溫度梯度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cross-section temperature curvature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲。這個失效與「截面溫度梯度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌頭與軌底溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending. This failure and a measurement bias in Cross-section temperature curvature can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail-head and rail-foot temperatures rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用軌頭與軌底溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲。這個失效與「截面溫度梯度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌頭與軌底溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending. This failure and a measurement bias in Cross-section temperature curvature can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail-head and rail-foot temperatures rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「截面溫度梯度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cross-section temperature curvature\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長","平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.","A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均溫度正常仍可能有差異熱彎曲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A normal mean temperature can coexist with differential thermal bending. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b340-v16-s5","title":"彈性釋放位移與軌斷缺口量級","titleEn":"Elastic release displacement & Broken-rail gap scale","description":"本階段聚焦「彈性釋放位移」與「軌斷缺口量級」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Elastic release displacement\" and \"Broken-rail gap scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b340-v16-33","title":"彈性釋放位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elastic release displacement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「彈性釋放位移」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elastic release displacement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"軸向彈性位移由軸力、長度與軸向剛度共同決定。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 10.3383 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻線彈性桿及固定面積；位移不含支承滑移、塑性或裂縫。使用模型載入卸載位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「彈性釋放位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Axial elastic movement depends on force, length and axial rigidity. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 10.3383 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. A uniform elastic bar with constant area; displacement excludes support slip, plasticity and cracking. Use loading-unloading movement in the model as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elastic release displacement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2；y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2; y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「彈性釋放位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elastic release displacement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-33-k1","title":"彈性釋放位移","titleEn":"Elastic release displacement","text":"軸向彈性位移由軸力、長度與軸向剛度共同決定。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 10.3383 mm。","textEn":"Axial elastic movement depends on force, length and axial rigidity. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「彈性釋放位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elastic release displacement\" is correct?","options":["軸向彈性位移由軸力、長度與軸向剛度共同決定。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一"],"optionsEn":["Axial elastic movement depends on force, length and axial rigidity.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line."],"answer":0,"explanation":"軸向彈性位移由軸力、長度與軸向剛度共同決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Axial elastic movement depends on force, length and axial rigidity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b340-v16-34","title":"彈性釋放位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Elastic release displacement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彈性釋放位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elastic release displacement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2；y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=10.3383 mm。模型邊界：均勻線彈性桿及固定面積；位移不含支承滑移、塑性或裂縫；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2; y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=10.3383 mm. Boundary: A uniform elastic bar with constant area; displacement excludes support slip, plasticity and cracking; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以模型載入卸載位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、兩端相對位移及卸載回復曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use loading-unloading movement in the model to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2；y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=10.3383 mm。模型邊界：均勻線彈性桿及固定面積；位移不含支承滑移、塑性或裂縫；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2; y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=10.3383 mm. Boundary: A uniform elastic bar with constant area; displacement excludes support slip, plasticity and cracking; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「彈性釋放位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elastic release displacement\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性溫度估錯會讓應力估計整體偏移","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單側日照造成的溫差會讓表面溫度失去代表性"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Incorrect neutral temperature shifts the full stress estimate.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2; y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One-sided sunshine makes a surface temperature unrepresentative."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2；y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, L=50 m, E=210 GPa, A=7600 mm2; y=F*1000*L/(E*1e9*A*1e-6)*1000=9.3985 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b340-v16-35","title":"彈性釋放位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elastic release displacement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彈性釋放位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elastic release displacement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以模型載入卸載位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、兩端相對位移及卸載回復曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「彈性釋放位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use loading-unloading movement in the model to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load model force gauge, relative endpoint displacement and unloading recovery, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Elastic release displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「彈性釋放位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻線彈性桿及固定面積；位移不含支承滑移、塑性或裂縫如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長造成偏離的合成觀察，以模型載入卸載位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Elastic release displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: A uniform elastic bar with constant area; displacement excludes support slip, plasticity and cracking. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic. Explain which evidence in loading-unloading movement in the model distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以模型載入卸載位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、兩端相對位移及卸載回復曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「彈性釋放位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use loading-unloading movement in the model to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load model force gauge, relative endpoint displacement and unloading recovery, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Elastic release displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「彈性釋放位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻線彈性桿及固定面積；位移不含支承滑移、塑性或裂縫如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長造成偏離的合成觀察，以模型載入卸載位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Elastic release displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: A uniform elastic bar with constant area; displacement excludes support slip, plasticity and cracking. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic. Explain which evidence in loading-unloading movement in the model distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「彈性釋放位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elastic release displacement\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：標距縮短後沿用原位移會放大推算溫差","本單元以模型載入卸載位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、兩端相對位移及卸載回復曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using the old displacement with a shorter gauge exaggerates inferred temperature change.","Use loading-unloading movement in the model to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以模型載入卸載位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型力計、兩端相對位移及卸載回復曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use loading-unloading movement in the model to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b340-v16-36","title":"彈性釋放位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elastic release displacement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彈性釋放位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elastic release displacement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長。這個失效與「彈性釋放位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查模型載入卸載位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic. This failure and a measurement bias in Elastic release displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check loading-unloading movement in the model rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用模型載入卸載位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長。這個失效與「彈性釋放位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查模型載入卸載位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic. This failure and a measurement bias in Elastic release displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check loading-unloading movement in the model rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彈性釋放位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elastic release displacement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一"],"optionsEn":["Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line."],"answer":0,"explanation":"支承滑移會使量到的位移不再全是彈性伸長。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Support slip means measured movement is not wholly elastic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b340-v16-37","title":"軌斷缺口量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Broken-rail gap scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「軌斷缺口量級」如何影響長焊鋼軌應力放散的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Broken-rail gap scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stress neutralization of continuously welded rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"釋放長度與溫差共同決定簡化缺口量級。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 15.18 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。長度是缺口兩側的總等效釋放長度；忽略分布摩擦與斷裂動態。使用缺口附近位移剖面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「軌斷缺口量級」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Released length and temperature difference jointly determine a reduced gap scale. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 15.18 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Length is the total effective released length on both sides of a gap; distributed friction and fracture dynamics are omitted. Use displacement profile near a gap as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Broken-rail gap scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「軌斷缺口量級」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Broken-rail gap scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-37-k1","title":"軌斷缺口量級","titleEn":"Broken-rail gap scale","text":"釋放長度與溫差共同決定簡化缺口量級。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 15.18 mm。","textEn":"Released length and temperature difference jointly determine a reduced gap scale. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軌斷缺口量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Broken-rail gap scale\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一","釋放長度與溫差共同決定簡化缺口量級。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line.","Released length and temperature difference jointly determine a reduced gap scale.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"釋放長度與溫差共同決定簡化缺口量級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Released length and temperature difference jointly determine a reduced gap scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b340-v16-38","title":"軌斷缺口量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Broken-rail gap scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軌斷缺口量級」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Broken-rail gap scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=15.18 mm。模型邊界：長度是缺口兩側的總等效釋放長度；忽略分布摩擦與斷裂動態；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=15.18 mm. Boundary: Length is the total effective released length on both sides of a gap; distributed friction and fracture dynamics are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以缺口附近位移剖面區分模型與觀察，先用合成缺口位移剖面、溫差及明列的兩側有效長度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use displacement profile near a gap to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=15.18 mm。模型邊界：長度是缺口兩側的總等效釋放長度；忽略分布摩擦與斷裂動態；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=15.18 mm. Boundary: Length is the total effective released length on both sides of a gap; distributed friction and fracture dynamics are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軌斷缺口量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Broken-rail gap scale\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗斷面仍沿用新軌面積會誤算軸力","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把滑動後阻力視為初始彈性剛度會混淆機制","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using new-rail area for worn rail miscalculates force.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing post-slip resistance with initial elastic stiffness mixes mechanisms.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.0000115 1/K, L=40 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=13.8 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b340-v16-39","title":"軌斷缺口量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Broken-rail gap scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「軌斷缺口量級」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Broken-rail gap scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以缺口附近位移剖面區分模型與觀察，先用合成缺口位移剖面、溫差及明列的兩側有效長度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌斷缺口量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use displacement profile near a gap to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic gap-displacement profile, temperature difference and declared effective lengths on both sides, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Broken-rail gap scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「軌斷缺口量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出長度是缺口兩側的總等效釋放長度；忽略分布摩擦與斷裂動態如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一造成偏離的合成觀察，以缺口附近位移剖面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Broken-rail gap scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Length is the total effective released length on both sides of a gap; distributed friction and fracture dynamics are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line. Explain which evidence in displacement profile near a gap distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以缺口附近位移剖面區分模型與觀察，先用合成缺口位移剖面、溫差及明列的兩側有效長度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌斷缺口量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use displacement profile near a gap to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic gap-displacement profile, temperature difference and declared effective lengths on both sides, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Broken-rail gap scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「軌斷缺口量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出長度是缺口兩側的總等效釋放長度；忽略分布摩擦與斷裂動態如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一造成偏離的合成觀察，以缺口附近位移剖面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Broken-rail gap scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Length is the total effective released length on both sides of a gap; distributed friction and fracture dynamics are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line. Explain which evidence in displacement profile near a gap distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軌斷缺口量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Broken-rail gap scale\"?","options":["本單元以缺口附近位移剖面區分模型與觀察，先用合成缺口位移剖面、溫差及明列的兩側有效長度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器熱漂移會被誤認為中性溫度改變"],"optionsEn":["Use displacement profile near a gap to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument thermal drift can resemble a neutral-temperature change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以缺口附近位移剖面區分模型與觀察，先用合成缺口位移剖面、溫差及明列的兩側有效長度建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use displacement profile near a gap to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b340-v16-40","title":"軌斷缺口量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Broken-rail gap scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b340-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軌斷缺口量級」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Broken-rail gap scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一。這個失效與「軌斷缺口量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查缺口附近位移剖面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line. This failure and a measurement bias in Broken-rail gap scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check displacement profile near a gap rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用缺口附近位移剖面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b340-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一。這個失效與「軌斷缺口量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查缺口附近位移剖面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line. This failure and a measurement bias in Broken-rail gap scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check displacement profile near a gap rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b340-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軌斷缺口量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Broken-rail gap scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部卡阻會破壞自由伸長假設"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local binding invalidates free-expansion behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只以缺口大小推算整條線軌應力並不唯一。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A gap size does not uniquely determine stress along an entire line. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b340-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b340-en.svg"}};
